 ## Background
-Parabolic Sphere Tracing was introduced in the paper "Parabolic Sphere Tracing of Signed Distance Fields for Old Glass Modelling and Rendering" [S1]. It is used for rendering heterogeneous media such as old glass panels, handling surface irregularities, bubbles, and complex transmitted caustics. The method leverages the analytical properties of parabolic trajectories to simplify ray tracing in media with linearly varying squared refractive index [S1].
